base-files: floor PKG_RELEASE above the published hotfix high-water mark

base-files derives PKG_RELEASE from COMMITCOUNT, which counts commits that
touch package/base-files.  That number does not move between our releases, so
every image we build ships the same base-files version -- 1719 today -- while
the hotfix channel has already served 1720.

apk compares version numbers, not contents.  Republishing 1720 with different
bytes makes an install of base-files=1720 a no-op on a device that already has
it, with no error anywhere; and an image shipping 1719 can never supersede a
hotfix published above it.  The release workflow now refuses to build an image
whose floor is not strictly higher than releases/<base>/published-versions.json,
so the failure is loud instead of silent.

Floor the number here.  Upstream count still wins once it passes the floor, so
this does not fork us from upstream permanently.

--- a/package/base-files/Makefile
+++ b/package/base-files/Makefile
@@ -13,7 +13,16 @@
 
 PKG_NAME:=base-files
 PKG_FLAGS:=nonshared
-PKG_RELEASE:=$(COMMITCOUNT)
+# The release number is the image's claim on this package, and apk compares
+# numbers, not contents.  Upstream derives it from COMMITCOUNT, which counts
+# commits touching package/base-files and does NOT move between our releases --
+# so a rebuilt image ships the same number as the last one and can never
+# outrank a hotfix already published above it.  Floor it, and let the release
+# workflow refuse to build an image whose floor is not strictly above the
+# published high-water mark (releases/<base>/published-versions.json).
+BASE_FILES_RELEASE_FLOOR:=1721
+BASE_FILES_COMMITCOUNT:=$(if $(COMMITCOUNT),$(COMMITCOUNT),0)
+PKG_RELEASE:=$(shell echo $$(( $(BASE_FILES_COMMITCOUNT) > $(BASE_FILES_RELEASE_FLOOR) ? $(BASE_FILES_COMMITCOUNT) : $(BASE_FILES_RELEASE_FLOOR) )))
 
 PKG_FILE_DEPENDS:=$(PLATFORM_DIR)/ $(GENERIC_PLATFORM_DIR)/base-files/
 PKG_BUILD_DEPENDS:=usign/host ucert/host
